From: Obsidience <local@obsidience>
Subject: [PATCH] launch: satisfy the QtWebEngine host contract

QtWebEngine initializes Chromium from QCoreApplication::arguments() and
rejects an empty argument list. Quickshell creates its GUI application with
an argument count of zero to hide the arguments it has already consumed, so
retain only the executable name.

QtWebEngine Quick also requires shared graphics contexts to be selected before
the application object exists. Set Qt's documented equivalent attribute,
Qt::AA_ShareOpenGLContexts, at the start of main().

Rebased onto Quickshell v0.3.2 (4f508be).

---
 src/launch/launch.cpp | 2 +-
 src/launch/main.cpp   | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/launch/launch.cpp b/src/launch/launch.cpp
index 1edd60c..e1de94b 100644
--- a/src/launch/launch.cpp
+++ b/src/launch/launch.cpp
@@ -280,7 +280,7 @@ int launch(const LaunchArgs& args, char** argv) {
 	QGuiApplication::setDesktopSettingsAware(pragmas.desktopSettingsAware);
 
 	QGuiApplication* app = nullptr;
-	auto qArgC = 0;
+	auto qArgC = 1;
 
 	if (pragmas.useQApplication) {
 		app = new QApplication(qArgC, argv);
diff --git a/src/launch/main.cpp b/src/launch/main.cpp
index 24969d8..ff6627a 100644
--- a/src/launch/main.cpp
+++ b/src/launch/main.cpp
@@ -117,6 +117,7 @@ void exitDaemon(int code) {
 }
 
 int main(int argc, char** argv) {
+	QCoreApplication::setAttribute(Qt::AA_ShareOpenGLContexts);
 	QCoreApplication::setApplicationName("quickshell");
 
 #if CRASH_HANDLER
